  "summary": "Malicious code in sc-payment-utils (npm)",
  "details": "Sc-payment-utils@9999.0.0 is a dependency-confusion package that exfiltrates system and CI-environment metadata on install. The preinstall hook (callback.js) collects hostname, username, current working directory, npm registry URL, and CI project identifiers (GITHUB_REPOSITORY, CI_PROJECT_PATH, TRAVIS_REPO_SLUG, and others) and sends them via HTTP GET to 75[.]119[.]137[.]232:31337/depconfuse. The package name mimics an internal utility and uses an inflated version number (9999.0.0) to take priority in dependency resolution.",
